lasso-mode
==========

lasso-mode is a derivative and aggregate work built on three MIT-licensed
open-source projects. Each is used under the terms of the MIT License.

1. pstack
   Author:  Lauren Tan (poteto)
   Source:  https://github.com/cursor/plugins/tree/main/pstack
   Commit:  e46364b8be46000b7df0f260550cd712afbb8d36
   Use:     The workflow engine. The router skill (lasso-mode), the 20
            principle skills, the 16 playbooks, and the workflow skills
            (how, why, architect, arena, interrogate, tdd, reflect, unslop,
            recall, blast-radius, figure-it-out, show-me-your-work,
            automate-me, typescript-best-practices, setup-lasso) are ported
            and adapted from pstack's poteto-mode. Cursor-specific details
            were adapted for Claude Code, and the cross-vendor multi-model
            review panels were reworked into single-provider, divergent-lens
            panels.

